  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_3' aria-label=\" Mohtashem Billah Malik versus Sana Aftab pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('3','2026','2026_2_352_361','2026INSC118'); ><font size='4'> <strong>MOHTASHEM BILLAH MALIK<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>SANA AFTAB </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 2 S.C.R. 352</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 118</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000432026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : PANKAJ MITHAL<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, SARASA VENKATANARAYANA BHATTI</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Matter pertains to the dispute regarding the custody of two minor sons born to the appellant-husband and the respondent-wife. Headnotes&dagger; Guardians and Wards Act, 1890 &ndash; s.25 &ndash; Custody of minors &ndash; Appellant-husband and respondent-wife, both Indian &ndash; Matrimonial dispute between them, culminating in divorce and the custody of the minors given to the wife while guardianship given to the husband by the Qatar court &ndash; Allegedly, the wife removed the minors from Qatar to India during their academic session, without the knowledge and<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 04-02-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CIVIL APPEAL No. 771/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Appeal(s) allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('3','2026','2026_2_352_361','2026INSC118','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a